<%- /*
SPDX-FileCopyrightText: 2026 Lusoris <lusoris@pm.me>
SPDX-License-Identifier: EUPL-1.2

Caller of the shared release-please workflow, as a consumer keeps it in
.github/workflows/release-please.yml. The rendered file is the whole of the
consumer's release-please job: the steps live in
.github/workflows/release-please.yml of the shared repository, named here by
commit with the version as a comment; before the first release the comment
carries no version (decision record 0024, decision record 0056).

Required check: none. The job runs on push to the default branch, never on a pull
request, and is no check of a pull request (cordanaLLM/praetor#1212 for the
name the engine declares). No result job is needed (decision record 0030).

The job acts through a GitHub App, not GITHUB_TOKEN: pull requests and
releases created with GITHUB_TOKEN start no workflows. The caller passes the
private key from its secret RELEASE_APP_PRIVATE_KEY and the client id from its
variable RELEASE_APP_CLIENT_ID.

Fields: .Shared.Repository, .Shared.Commit and .Shared.Version are working
names until the engine renders caller templates (cordanaLLM/praetor#1211);
.RunnerTag is the engine's own.

Concurrency is set here and not in the shared workflow, so a consumer's group
never collides with another caller's.

Licence header: the rendered caller starts with the consumer's own header,
written from .Licence (working names, as above), so the consumer's licence
check accepts it (#3). The REUSE-IgnoreStart and REUSE-IgnoreEnd notes render
as nothing and keep this repository's licence check from reading the field
lines as tags.
*/ -%>
<%- /* REUSE-IgnoreStart */ -%>
# SPDX-FileCopyrightText: <% .Licence.CopyrightText %>
# SPDX-License-Identifier: <% .Licence.Identifier %>
<%/* REUSE-IgnoreEnd */ -%>
---
# Release please: proposes release pull requests and creates forge releases.
# The job is the shared workflow of <% .Shared.Repository %>, named by commit.
name: Release please

on:
  push:
    branches: [main]

permissions: {}

concurrency:
  group: release-please-${{ github.ref }}
  cancel-in-progress: false

jobs:
  release-please:
    name: Release please
    permissions: {}
    uses: <% .Shared.Repository %>/.github/workflows/release-please.yml@<% .Shared.Commit %> # <% .Shared.Version %>
    with:
      runner: <% .RunnerTag %>
      app_client_id: ${{ vars.RELEASE_APP_CLIENT_ID }}
    secrets:
      app_private_key: ${{ secrets.RELEASE_APP_PRIVATE_KEY }}
